Branch 4 (the "App") respects your privacy. This policy explains what
information the App handles.

1. Information we do not collect

The App does not require an account or sign-in. It does not collect or
transmit personally identifiable information such as your name, email
address, phone number, or location.

2. Information stored on your device only

Your game progress (week, staff, budget, settings) is stored solely on
your device. It is never transmitted elsewhere and is removed when you
delete the App. No server operated for this App can access it.

3. Advertising

The App uses Google AdMob to serve rewarded ads. Ads play only when you
choose to watch one.

In the course of serving ads, AdMob may collect your advertising
identifier (IDFA), device information, and approximate location. This is
collected and processed by Google. The App does not read or retain that
information.

Google's practices: https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites

4. Tracking consent

On iOS, you are asked for tracking permission before the first ad plays.
Declining does not affect your ability to watch ads or receive rewards;
you will simply be shown non-personalised ads.

You may change this at any time in Settings > Privacy & Security >
Tracking on your device.

5. Notifications

The App may use device notifications to tell you when a week has ended.
Notifications are scheduled and shown on your device; no information is
sent anywhere.

You can turn notifications off in your device settings.

6. Children

The App is not directed at children under 14, and we do not knowingly
collect personal information from children.

7. Changes to this policy

If this policy changes, the revised version and its date will be posted
on this page.

